1
00:00:01,256 --> 00:00:04,566
"The Cheerleader"

2
00:00:05,621 --> 00:00:06,970
<i>Out here
in the middle,</i>

3
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:08,660
<i>people are straight shooters.</i>

4
00:00:08,695 --> 00:00:10,345
<i>They just say it
like it is.</i>

5
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:17,526
<i>Well, I got one of those types
in my house as well.</i>

6
00:00:17,610 --> 00:00:19,070
Hell, yeah,
you were a mistake.

7
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:20,450
I mean, we're happy
that you're here now,

8
00:00:20,570 --> 00:00:22,008
but you were
definitely a mistake.

9
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,520
It's funny,
'cause you're not fat,

10
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,990
but that skirt
sure makes you look fat.

11
00:00:26,140 --> 00:00:28,214
Who told you
Scrappy went to a farm?

12
00:00:28,410 --> 00:00:30,052
He's not on a farm.
He's dead.

13
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:33,551
Oh, hey, Dad,

14
00:00:33,680 --> 00:00:35,410
I'm trying out
for swim team.

15
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:37,609
Do you want to come watch me
swim laps at the pool?

16
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,060
- Sounds boring.
- Mike.

17
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,400
- It does.
- Mike.

18
00:00:40,530 --> 00:00:43,646
You saying my name over and over
doesn't make it sound less boring.

19
00:00:44,160 --> 00:00:46,360
<i>But sometimes the family
needs more than honesty.</i>

20
00:00:46,490 --> 00:00:49,461
<i>It needs a cheerleader,
and that's me.</i>

21
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:52,144
You know, Sue, I think
what your dad is saying

22
00:00:52,179 --> 00:00:53,930
is it sounds like
a lot of fun.

23
00:00:55,584 --> 00:00:58,334
The dryer's making
that noise again.

24
00:00:58,650 --> 00:01:00,011
<i>Noise again.</i>

25
00:01:00,380 --> 00:01:02,860
What noise?
Your dad fixed it.

26
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,468
It's working great now.

27
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:08,779
Damn thing's
on its last legs.

28
00:01:08,810 --> 00:01:09,749
I can't hear the TV.

29
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:13,018
No, we can't afford a new
dryer right now. It's fine.

30
00:01:13,890 --> 00:01:15,267
Did anybody get the mail?

31
00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:16,610
Get more pop.

32
00:01:16,760 --> 00:01:18,986
Axl, come on.
Let's go.

33
00:01:19,140 --> 00:01:20,950
<i>Axl had told us
he was at church group</i>

34
00:01:20,985 --> 00:01:22,661
<i>when he was actually
sticking his tongue</i>

35
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:24,345
<i>down some girl's throat
at the mall.</i>

36
00:01:24,620 --> 00:01:27,479
<i>So he'd earned himself one of
Mike's famous punishments--</i>

37
00:01:27,590 --> 00:01:28,565
<i>For the next two weeks,</i>

38
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,605
<i>he had to stay within 5 feet
of a parent at all times.</i>

39
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,661
Oh, my God, Mike.
It's 2009.

40
00:01:40,790 --> 00:01:42,100
What?! Already?

41
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:44,078
Yeah, Mike. 2009.

42
00:01:44,330 --> 00:01:45,752
How did this happen?

43
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,203
No payments till 2009.

44
00:01:50,440 --> 00:01:52,425
No payments till 2009.

45
00:01:54,010 --> 00:01:56,230
No payments till 2009.

46
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:58,964
The economy's gonna be
great by then.

47
00:01:59,550 --> 00:02:00,990
Great.
Now with interest,

48
00:02:01,025 --> 00:02:03,192
we owe $650 on a VCR

49
00:02:03,242 --> 00:02:05,587
we sold at the garage sale
last year for 2 bucks.

50
00:02:07,950 --> 00:02:09,031
You know what?

51
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:10,298
It'll be fine.

52
00:02:10,690 --> 00:02:11,680
It's fine.

53
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:13,738
It'll be fine.
We're fine.

54
00:02:13,970 --> 00:02:16,700
These things have a way
of working themselves out.

55
00:02:16,735 --> 00:02:19,484
As long as the dryer hangs on
and I sell a car this month,

56
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:21,300
we're gonna be fine.

57
00:02:31,110 --> 00:02:34,364
<i>Fortunately, out here, you always
have neighbors you can count on...</i>

58
00:02:37,150 --> 00:02:41,080
Hi. Would it be okay if I
just threw in a quick dry?

59
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:46,115
Hi. Hate to bother.
Just one more quick load?

60
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,220
And when that fails...

61
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:52,475
Hello? Hello? I'm hurt,
and my mom and dad aren't home.

62
00:02:55,420 --> 00:02:58,096
I'll just do this quick load
while you try to find them.

63
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,062
You won't even know
I'm here.

64
00:03:01,850 --> 00:03:04,537
<i>So the busted dryer piled
on to the whole 2009 thing</i>

65
00:03:04,572 --> 00:03:06,553
<i>meant we were gonna have
to cut corners fast.</i>

66
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,820
<i>First up,
a trip to the Frugal Hoosier,</i>

67
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:11,300
<i>Indiana's number one
expired food store.</i>

68
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:16,680
So are we, like,
poor now?

69
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:18,420
No, we're not poor.
We're just thrifty.

70
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:21,031
We're trying something new
called living within our means.

71
00:03:21,066 --> 00:03:22,523
You mean we've been
living outside our means?

72
00:03:23,030 --> 00:03:24,120
Oh, God.

73
00:03:24,250 --> 00:03:25,800
You should be thanking me.

74
00:03:25,940 --> 00:03:29,437
Listen, smart consumers--
They're the kids who are popular.

75
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:32,000
Brick, shake some
of those unmarked cans

76
00:03:32,140 --> 00:03:33,780
and see if you can find peas.
Okay?

77
00:03:33,930 --> 00:03:35,566
We're listening for peas,
people.

78
00:03:35,680 --> 00:03:36,730
Hi, Bob.

79
00:03:36,900 --> 00:03:38,500
Frankie, hi.
It's me, Bob.

80
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:40,550
Listen, Ehlert is
throwing a major hissy.

81
00:03:40,650 --> 00:03:43,015
He's calling everybody in for
some emergency meeting at 1:00.

82
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:45,580
1:00? Are you kidding me?
I was barely making it at 3:00.

83
00:03:45,615 --> 00:03:46,520
Unh-unh. No fish.

84
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:47,421
<i>You've gotta
get in here.</i>

85
00:03:47,473 --> 00:03:48,450
I don't know
what it's about,

86
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,980
and I'm--I'm just
freaking out here.

87
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,587
Okay, I'll call Mike
at the quarry

88
00:03:51,637 --> 00:03:52,670
and figure something out
with the kids.

89
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,103
I'll be there as soon as I can.
Just breathe.

90
00:03:55,570 --> 00:03:57,970
Okay, kids, new plan.
Gotta get to work early.

91
00:03:58,110 --> 00:03:59,276
But what about the pool?

92
00:03:59,390 --> 00:04:01,905
You promised you'd watch me
practice for swim tryouts.

93
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:04,054
And you said you would
take me to the library.

94
00:04:04,120 --> 00:04:05,354
"The Wheel of Nuldoid"--

95
00:04:05,404 --> 00:04:07,580
I have to check it out
before anybody else gets it.

96
00:04:07,710 --> 00:04:09,171
You promised.

97
00:04:09,353 --> 00:04:10,610
<i>Promised.</i>

98
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:13,767
Okay, I know I didn't promise that
many things. I'm not that nice.

99
00:04:14,070 --> 00:04:15,880
Listen, we'll swing
by the library,

100
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:17,420
and then when your father
gets home from work,

101
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:18,730
he'll take you
to the pool.

102
00:04:18,765 --> 00:04:21,067
But if you kids ever want
to eat name brand food again,

103
00:04:21,102 --> 00:04:21,954
I have to get to work.

104
00:04:22,024 --> 00:04:23,090
Come on.
Let's move it.

105
00:04:23,250 --> 00:04:26,010
I love this book.
I love this book. I love this book.

106
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,060
I hate my life.
I hate my life. I ha--

107
00:04:28,190 --> 00:04:30,489
You got 5 feet, mister.
Use all of it.

108
00:04:31,530 --> 00:04:33,700
Uh-oh. You have a fine.

109
00:04:34,210 --> 00:04:36,199
Oh, that's no problem.
How much?

110
00:04:36,234 --> 00:04:37,052
We're in kind of a hurry.

111
00:04:37,210 --> 00:04:39,089
$189.

112
00:04:39,530 --> 00:04:40,585
You're kidding.

113
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:42,924
I'm sorry,
but there is no way

114
00:04:42,959 --> 00:04:44,490
that we can pay
that fine right now.

115
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:46,210
I mean,
our dryer just broke,

116
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:48,982
and I haven't sold a car,
and it's 2009.

117
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:51,274
Right.
Next in line.

118
00:04:51,670 --> 00:04:52,890
Mom, don't they know
who you are?

119
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,896
Flash her
your Frugal Hoosier card.

120
00:04:56,930 --> 00:05:00,081
Listen, my son
is a very odd kid.

121
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,840
Books
are everything to him.

122
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,448
He has no friends.

123
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:07,581
I'm sorry,
but until you pay the fine,

124
00:05:07,616 --> 00:05:08,479
you're banned.

125
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:11,804
Oh... and your library
card has been flagged.

126
00:05:12,590 --> 00:05:14,068
Have a nice day.

127
00:05:16,510 --> 00:05:17,366
You know what?

128
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:18,660
This is a good thing.

129
00:05:18,695 --> 00:05:21,088
Your teacher says you need
more social interaction.

130
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:23,140
And besides,
you're not watching enough TV.

131
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,435
You don't want
to be the only kid

132
00:05:24,495 --> 00:05:26,162
who doesn't know
who won "The Bachelor."

133
00:05:26,330 --> 00:05:28,498
<i>Yep, there I was,
still cheerleading,</i>

134
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:32,080
<i>from a hole getting so deep
I could barely see the sky.</i>

135
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:33,790
Hey, did
you cover for me?

136
00:05:33,930 --> 00:05:35,490
I told them that you had a
pregnancy scare on the way in

137
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,254
and also that
you burst an aneurysm.

138
00:05:37,626 --> 00:05:40,185
You should know that I do
not think he bought it.

139
00:05:41,140 --> 00:05:42,132
Curler.

140
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:46,860
But trailing even the most pathetic
of you is our newest employee,

141
00:05:47,010 --> 00:05:48,117
Frances Heck.

142
00:05:48,450 --> 00:05:51,320
Her sales record
is minus one.

143
00:05:51,770 --> 00:05:54,042
<i>Negative uno vehiculo--</i>

144
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:56,410
That's mexican for
"not good."

145
00:05:56,550 --> 00:05:58,472
Well, you know,
there is recession on.

146
00:05:58,610 --> 00:06:00,670
Enough of
your Communist whining.

147
00:06:00,810 --> 00:06:02,590
It's always somebody else's fault--

148
00:06:02,740 --> 00:06:06,020
the economy,
your mama didn't breast-feed you,

149
00:06:06,150 --> 00:06:08,710
the government won't let you
marry a houseplant.

150
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:12,840
Now I want to hear some
suggestions to perk up business.

151
00:06:12,980 --> 00:06:15,380
And don't anybody
say free mugs.

152
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:18,922
Well, I'll throw
your stragglers a bone.

153
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:21,388
How about a free AK-47
with every sale?

154
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:22,553
People love guns.

155
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:25,493
You really want
to arm our customers?

156
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:27,962
Anybody else?

157
00:06:28,020 --> 00:06:29,834
Oh! Here's a thought--

158
00:06:30,300 --> 00:06:31,830
I was just in
the Frugal Hoosier,

159
00:06:31,970 --> 00:06:34,212
and they have these Ronald Reagan
inaugural jelly beans--

160
00:06:34,247 --> 00:06:35,340
50 cents a bag.

161
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:36,628
How about we fill
a car with them

162
00:06:36,678 --> 00:06:38,325
and let people guess
how many for a prize?

163
00:06:38,620 --> 00:06:40,080
I don't know.
Thought it'd be fun.

164
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:43,641
Hmm. Clever...

165
00:06:44,660 --> 00:06:45,624
Patriotic...

166
00:06:46,220 --> 00:06:46,950
Cheap.

167
00:06:48,380 --> 00:06:50,947
You know, I was gonna fire you
right after the meeting,

168
00:06:51,310 --> 00:06:55,438
but I think I'll just move
that Post-It to next week.

169
00:06:59,000 --> 00:06:59,973
Hear that, Pete?

170
00:07:00,034 --> 00:07:02,322
Not fired for another week.
Yeah, baby.

171
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:07,660
<i>So while I was busy hanging on
to my job by my fingernails...</i>

172
00:07:07,810 --> 00:07:08,540
Yeah, so good.

173
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,400
Cannonball!

174
00:07:09,530 --> 00:07:11,750
<i>At least I knew
my family was having fun

175
00:07:11,785 --> 00:07:13,153
<i>at the Orson Aquatorium.</i>

176
00:07:13,260 --> 00:07:14,251
Axl, you getting in?

177
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,308
Pool's queer.

178
00:07:16,580 --> 00:07:18,220
Brick, how about you?
You getting in?

179
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,113
Swimming's no fun
without a book.

180
00:07:20,610 --> 00:07:22,291
Then what the hell
am I doing here?

181
00:07:22,860 --> 00:07:24,103
Come on, Brick.
Look at those boys.

182
00:07:24,205 --> 00:07:25,021
They're having fun.

183
00:07:28,780 --> 00:07:30,720
Mom says
I'm supposed to interact.

184
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:32,596
So can I tell you
the plot of the book

185
00:07:32,631 --> 00:07:34,211
I wasn't allowed
to check out?

186
00:07:34,390 --> 00:07:36,911
Chapter one:
"Grampa's Story."

187
00:07:37,060 --> 00:07:39,200
"Grampa Worst
was old and dying--"

188
00:07:39,330 --> 00:07:40,181
Oh! Oh, daddy!

189
00:07:40,213 --> 00:07:41,660
I'm ready for you
to watch me swim now.

190
00:07:41,820 --> 00:07:43,043
Hey, finally.

191
00:07:43,390 --> 00:07:45,445
At least one of my kids is
actually getting in the pool.

192
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:47,640
"He was dying of something
old people die of."

193
00:07:47,780 --> 00:07:48,643
So you got it.

194
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:52,755
All right, Sue! Come on, kid.
Show us how it's done.

195
00:08:11,170 --> 00:08:12,226
Hi, guys!

196
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,780
Did you have fun
at the pool?

197
00:08:13,940 --> 00:08:16,307
Dad said that
I suck at swimming

198
00:08:16,437 --> 00:08:20,013
and I shouldn't try out
for swim team.

199
00:08:20,640 --> 00:08:22,531
Then I bought you
a creamsicle.

200
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:28,480
So then the Nuldoids
kidnap this kid

201
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,724
and take him
to the bowels of the Earth.

202
00:08:30,759 --> 00:08:32,310
Speaking of bowels,
what's for dinner?

203
00:08:32,430 --> 00:08:33,618
Hey, no complaints.

204
00:08:33,619 --> 00:08:35,810
That chicken or beef stew
last night was great,

205
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,270
and we all kept
that down.

206
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:38,880
<i>Not completely true.</i>

207
00:08:39,010 --> 00:08:40,730
And after
the giant tunnel hole,

208
00:08:40,850 --> 00:08:43,940
they go to the ancient slide
of the Droiden Frobble dynasty.

209
00:08:44,070 --> 00:08:46,880
Okay, Brick, honey,
great social interaction today.

210
00:08:47,010 --> 00:08:48,320
Now please go find a book.

211
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,497
There must be one book in
the house you haven't read.

212
00:08:50,860 --> 00:08:51,722
Okay.

213
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,775
Hey, champ.

214
00:08:54,740 --> 00:08:57,163
Mom says I've had enough
social interaction today.

215
00:08:57,560 --> 00:08:59,511
Okay. Catch you later.

216
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,360
<i>I was still mad at Mike,</i>

217
00:09:01,510 --> 00:09:03,438
<i>but I have
a pretty good poker face.</i>

218
00:09:04,670 --> 00:09:06,055
Frankie, you weren't there.

219
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,464
You weren't at the pool.
She was bad. She was...

220
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:11,488
rhythmic dance team
tryout bad.

221
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:14,530
All right, well,
just because she sucks

222
00:09:14,660 --> 00:09:16,430
doesn't mean you should
tell her that she sucks.

223
00:09:16,465 --> 00:09:18,217
What do you think that
does for her self-esteem?

224
00:09:18,252 --> 00:09:20,030
You know, I thought I was
taking 'em to the pool.

225
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,205
If I had known it was gonna be
anything about self-esteem,

226
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:23,228
I wouldn't have done it.

227
00:09:24,810 --> 00:09:25,730
What do you want?

228
00:09:25,850 --> 00:09:26,686
5 feet, Dad.

229
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:33,765
What should I have
done, Frankie--

230
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,416
Lie to her?

231
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:36,816
Since when did telling
the truth become a bad thing?

232
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:40,200
Sue's a sensitive young girl
who needs to be treated delicately.

233
00:09:40,410 --> 00:09:42,470
Her emotions
are right on the surface.

234
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:43,934
She's not Axl.

235
00:09:47,740 --> 00:09:49,010
We're her parents, Mike.

236
00:09:49,150 --> 00:09:52,023
It's our job to cheer her on,
no matter what.

237
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,320
Hey, I love my daughter,

238
00:09:53,450 --> 00:09:54,780
and I'm not gonna
have her made fun of.

239
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,238
If someone's gonna
dash her hopes,

240
00:09:56,273 --> 00:09:57,601
damn it,
it should be her family.

241
00:09:58,570 --> 00:10:00,641
Mom, Dad,
guess what?

242
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,390
They did an eye test
today at school,

243
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,087
and I need glasses.

244
00:10:05,300 --> 00:10:08,450
<i>In retrospect,
I guess there were signs.</i>

245
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:12,786
Oh, I only want one.
I don't need both of them,

246
00:10:12,950 --> 00:10:13,714
but thanks.

247
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:14,544
I got it!

